Falsifies `system_tests::user::nth_retype_tests::the_nth_retype_fails_as_an_empty_region_would_and_no_other`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64 (the hunk is portable kernel code).

The defect: `memory_region::split` loses its hook, so a `SPLIT` is neither counted nor ever
failed. A program's splits would then never reach their failure paths under a sweep, and the sweep
would say nothing about it.

Expected to fail: `arming retype 1 of 3`, the tally reading `seen: 2` where three retypes were
made. Replayed red on aarch64 on 2026-10-04 (UTC) by the lane for milestone 757 (a test kernel
fails a process on its Nth retype).

